This visa is for individuals who intend to visit Papua New Guinea provide entertainment as a comedian for commercial purposes.To be issued this visa, persons entering Papua New Guinea must be engaged in these activities for commercial purposes:-

Provide entertainment as a Comedian;
Conduct site visits and stage setups;
Attend scheduled business meetings with authorized agencies and clients;

This visa is for individuals who intend to visit Papua New Guinea to conduct permissible business activities and attend meetings that do not constitute labour or employment. To be issued this visa, persons entering Papua New Guinea must be engaged in one of the following business activities:-

Attend business meetings;
Attend workshops and conferences;
Facilitating in a workshop or conference or Training;
Conduct an exploratory business visit or participate in business negotiations;
To negotiate or discuss the set-up, expansion or wind-up of a business in Papua New Guinea;
To carry out any business with the authorised representatives of an overseas company, body or person;
Job interview and recruitment of manpower or
Tour guides and operators

Long term: If you are a student and wish to study in South Africa you can apply for a study visa by completing Form BI-1738.

Visas issued for studies at higher education and training institution shall be issued for duration of the course, but not exceeding four years;

Visas issued for studies at school shall be valid for the duration of the studies; provided that the duration for studies at the primary school shall not exceed eight years and for secondary school shall not exceed five years.
